-- STEP 16: Dashboard/Assessments/Reports tab APP_CONTROLS (RESOURCE_ID 834/835/836)
-- ============================================================
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- IT Operations Maturity - per-tab APP_CONTROLS / APP_ACCESS_CONTROLS rows
-- for Dashboard, Assessments, and Reports - same CSM-standard mechanism the
-- rest of the platform already uses for tab visibility (see
-- ITOperationMaturity_AppControl.sql for RESOURCE_ID 830, the parent "IT
-- Operations Maturity" tile itself).
--
-- This governs TAB VISIBILITY only (whether the Dashboard/Assessments/
-- Reports links even render in the nav bar), via EMP_INFO.CSM_TITLE_ID
-- (APP_ACCESS_CONTROLS.ROLE_ID) same as every other CSM tab. It does NOT
-- change what DATA a visible tab actually shows once opened - that stays
-- entirely governed by the existing ITOps logic already in
-- ITOperationMaturityController.cs (Superuser / Assessor / Assessee /
-- Reviewer / GDH / project allocation / the 6 PROJECT ownership columns).
-- A user can see an empty Dashboard/Reports/Assessments tab with nothing in
-- it if their title grants VIEW_ACCESS here but none of that data-layer
-- membership applies to them - same as how Reports already behaved before
-- this script (no gate on the tab, but nothing to show without real access).
--
-- Access is granted broadly (VIEW_ACCESS = 1 for every CSM title) on first
-- install, same broadened state RESOURCE_ID 830 itself already ended up in
-- (see ITOperationMaturity_V2_27_NavIconBroadAccess.sql) - restricting
-- specific titles later is then just an UPDATE on these rows' VIEW_ACCESS,
-- no code change needed.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

